    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d398-a2">

                <pb facs="0596" n="502" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg502"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    285.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Governor-General of the Amoor to Mr.
                        Breckinridge.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-04-02"><hi rendition="#small-caps">April</hi> 2/14,
                            1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: In reply to your letter of March 28
                    (April 9) I beg to inform you that Prince Lobanow-Rostowsky, when referring you
                    to me, was not aware of the tact that all affairs pertaining to the industry in
                    the waters of the Tülen (Seals) Island is under the jurisdiction of the ministry
                    of marine; it will therefore be necessary for you to apply to Admiral
                    Tchikatcheff.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. Doukovskoy.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
